## Criteria and verdicts

{% include 'shared/_criterion_verification_procedure.j2' %}

Use one stable `PA-###` item per fixed criterion in `## Criterion Verdicts`. Include `Step: [S-n]` with the canonical step ID or `Plan-level:`, then `Criterion:`, `Expected observation:`, `Observation:`, `Verdict:`, `Evidence:`, `Location:`, and `Cost:`. `completed` requires every criterion to be `met` with evidence and no counterexample found. For `request_changes` or `failed`, mirror each localized non-met verdict in `## What Came Up Short`; do not add `How To Fix`. A `not evaluable` criterion requires `failed`.

### Parallel structure

For `## Work Units` or `## Parallel Plan`, check parallel structure as a
first-class criterion: distinct responsibilities and a workable coordination
strategy. Directory disjointness and exact-file ownership are useful dispatch
options, not requirements for plan acceptance. Units may share directories
or even files; check that their work areas are distinct and shared edits can
be integrated without lost changes. Responsibility paths are optional.
Check no reserved `.`, `.git`, or `.agent` ownership;
every cross-unit dependency names a declared unit and every actual cross-unit
prerequisite has a `Depends on:` edge; and no cycles or inconsistent step
dependencies. The unit count must not exceed the effective active policy cap
of {{ WORK_UNITS_MAX_CAP|default('32') }} (`max_work_units`). `max_parallel_workers`
limits concurrent execution; queued units are valid. `## Parallel Plan` may
use disjoint `Paths:` files in the same directory. Shared contracts, interfaces, and schemas must be fixed
before dependent writers start, without delaying unrelated branches.
Check every ordering edge for a concrete prerequisite. Unnecessary serialization
through invented dependencies or explicit serial scheduling violates the
parallel-default requirement: record the unmet criterion with reproducible
step evidence and return `request_changes`. A step plan without Work Units
is valid when independent steps remain concurrently schedulable, including
file-disjoint groups whose directories overlap. Do not fail for heading shape.
Delegate independent command-resolution checks and criterion groups to
read-only subagents and reconcile their reproducible findings here.

